you can't make an omelet without  breaking a few eggs and you can't become  the number one drama on television  without generating at least a little bit  of off-screen drama that's certainly the  case with NCIS the hit procedural might  be popular now but it wasn't an easy  path what went on behind the scenes to  make this one of the highest-rated shows  on television that's a question worthy  of its own investigation title troubles  few people remember it now  but when NCIS first spun off from parent  show jag in 2003 it was far from a  guaranteed success in fact CBS was  worried that the show would be  overshadowed by the network's runaway  smash CSI  so CBS called the show Navy NCIS for the  first season in order to minimize  confusion over the similar acronyms  showrunner and creator Donald Belisario  eventually came in to the network to  drop the Navy part because it's totally  redundant the N in NCIS already stands  for naval it's a lot to keep track of us  mark Harmon's rage Bellisario abruptly  left NCIS in 2007 for a very unexpected  reason star Mark Harmon forced him out  reportedly the two tangled behind the  scenes for months over Harmons  dissatisfaction with Belisarius chaotic  management style it led to a showdown  and the network decided they could live  without Belisario who was forced to  resign the show continued with the  presumably happy Harmon sitting pretty  Belisario still got the last word  however NCIS lawsuit Angelus given the  huge success of NCIS it seems like a  no-brainer that would eventually spawn a  spinoff but the creation of NCIS Los  Angeles in 2009 actually led to a major  lawsuit that's because NCIS creator  Donald Belisario had a clause in his  contract giving him the right to create  the first spin-off after he was forced  off the show  CBS hired Shane Brennan to create the  offshoot show instead after years of  legal wrestling is settled out of court  for an undisclosed amount at an  estimated net worth of 250 million  dollars Belisario certainly isn't  suffering either way and CIS bred in  2013 NCIS was poised to add yet another  series to its franchise in the form of  NCIS red introduced in a two-episode arc  on NCIS Los Angeles NCIS red was going  to star John Corbett as the leader of  red team an anti-terrorist unit within  and C is one NCIS team  the network decided they didn't really  dig what they saw in the backdoor pilot  and the series was cancelled before it  ever began instead the network launched  NCIS New Orleans Don Johnson almost Mark  Harmon has been the face of NCIS for  well over a decade now but viewers could  have actually seen a very different face  in the role of agent Leroy Gibbs that's  because the role was actually offered to  Don Johnson first and he turned it down  he wasn't the only candidate though  rumor has it that NCIS New Orleans star  Scott Bakula was also on the original  shortlist for agent Gibbs way back in  the day since Belisario and Bakula had  previously worked together on quantum  leap by the time NCIS New Orleans came  along the showrunners knew the right man  for the job was vacuumed uh because he's  spectacular pauley perrette twitter  blunder in 2013 actress cote de pablo  who played fan favorite NCIS agent Ziva  de vivre abruptly announced her  departure from the show it was a  surprise not only to fans but to her  co-stars around the same time her red  posted a tweet of herself wearing a  shirt she received in 2007 which said I  love my job  it seemed innocent enough but it set off  a minor Twitter war with de Pablo's fans  who saw it as an attack allegedly the  Pablo called Perez to ask that she  stopped tweeting about the situation  Barret shut down her feed for less than  a day she should have just won the shirt  his daddy Koretz personal life while  Perron has clearly been a subject of  real-world drama she's done her best to  turn lemons into lemonade by using her  position as a platform for advocacy in  2006 she revealed that her former  husband Francis coyote shivers had  subjected 30 years of physical and  emotional abuse and just in 2015 after  she was randomly attacked by a mentally  ill homeless man she began championing  the rights of the homeless distri really  super great well to be alive but the  other part is that like my heart breaks  for that guy and and it breaks for every  single person that's out there on the  street she's also stood up for marriage  equality and even recorded music with a  positive message for victims of abuse  Diane Neal's Twitter meltdown in 2015  guest-starred Diane Nia launched an  angry Twitter attack on NCIS New Orleans  upset over safety issues she encountered  on set while filming Neil called the  show's production dangerous and stupid  saying stuff like they just used me like  a rented mule  and these folks don't give a damn didn't  go over well behind the scenes Neil  apologized and deleted the tweets some  certified folks on reddit captured the  drama and preserved it for posterity  however moral the story never tweet  angry a very important cameo with three  different shows and more than twenty  combined seasons the NCIS franchise has  had a lot of high-profile guest stars  but none of them can quite match the  star power our First Lady Michelle Obama  who appeared as herself on the series in  early 2016  her appearance was made in support of  joining forces a nationwide initiative  supporting service members veterans and  their families kind of makes that time  Taylor Swift showed up on CSI seemed  pretty lame by comparison thanks for  watching subscribe to our YouTube  channel to watch more videos like the  one you just saw and leave us a comment  to let us know what you've heard about  NCIS
 

